[5] Theorem-facing update
  Covering-moment discharge should be stated as a family theorem for
  nested-refinement / owner-transition gamma-Node3 packets, not as raw positivity.
  After THM-573, this family theorem only needs the <=6-multiples-of-7 residual.
  K33 discharge should be stated as construction of a THM-572 lift from
  cross-handoff packets.  Failure to build the lift feeds back as a
  missing localized covering-moment sidecar.
